WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.640
Buying a small business is one of
the oldest ways to build wealth.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.260
You buy a company that already makes
money, mostly with borrowed money,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.520
and its profits pay the loan back.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:19.887
Our example company earns one million
dollars a year and sells for four times that:

00:00:19.927 --> 00:00:20.627
four million.

00:00:21.307 --> 00:00:26.627
With closing costs and a cash cushion, the
project is four point two five million.

00:00:27.247 --> 00:00:30.147
An SBA bank loan covers ninety percent.

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:34.667
The seller lends five percent
and waits until the bank is paid.

00:00:35.347 --> 00:00:38.167
You bring the last five percent in cash.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:42.947
That last block is the
rule new buyers miss.

00:00:43.587 --> 00:00:47.407
Under the SBA's newest rulebook,
as one lending broker reads it,

00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:51.767
at least half of the ten percent
down payment must be your own cash.

00:00:52.287 --> 00:00:56.627
So two hundred fifty thousand dollars
supports a project of about five million.

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.433
This is a leveraged buyout.

00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:05.173
The business throws off about eight
hundred thousand dollars a year after taxes

00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:06.313
and upkeep.

00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:08.973
The loan payment takes
about six hundred thousand,

00:01:09.353 --> 00:01:11.513
and the balance shrinks every year.

00:01:12.173 --> 00:01:16.513
With flat earnings, your stake is worth
about one point three five million after

00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:17.413
five years.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:22.493
Grow earnings five percent a year, and
it's about two point four five million.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.780
Now say the seller wants five million.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:30.580
The loan payment jumps to about
seven hundred forty thousand,

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:34.880
and the bank's coverage ratio
falls to one point oh eight.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.020
Banks want at least one point two five.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:43.280
Two fixes: raise about six hundred
fifty thousand dollars from investors,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.140
or bring the price down to
about four point three million.

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:53.147
Investors usually ask for an eight
to twelve percent preferred return,

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:58.307
their money back first, and a bigger
share than their dollars alone would buy.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:03.267
Here they'd own about a quarter of the
company and earn about twenty-four percent

00:02:03.287 --> 00:02:08.067
a year if earnings stay flat, short
of the thirty percent they target.

00:02:08.907 --> 00:02:11.687
Often the cheapest money in
a deal is a better price.
